A demonstrated fill establishes only that the particular enclosed interior in that pair changes to the observed color. In a fresh grid with multiple closed outlines, especially outlines of different colors or dimensions, do not extrapolate that every cavity is selected. Inventory each cavity and compare boundary color, geometry, and interior against the demonstrated case. Preserve the border and exterior, and change only interiors supported by the rule. If the available demo does not distinguish candidate selectors (for example, one eligible-color outline versus another-color outline), spend a demo request on that ambiguity before submitting.

This lesson arose in a task-67c59573 recurrence: one demo showed a color-6 rectangular outline's background interior becoming 7; the test also included color-5 rectangular outlines. Two submissions filled both types, with differing scope, and were incorrect. The demos did not establish that the color-5 cavities should be filled, so this is a warning about overgeneralization, not a solved selection rule.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/HA-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/held-out/play/users/u043/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-interaction-discipline/references/outline-color-scope.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-solving", "file": "references/compact-output-interpretation.md", "content": "# Interpreting compact ARC outputs

When demonstrations map a larger grid to a small output, treat the output as a structured encoding rather than an arbitrary answer shape. For every demo, establish:

- what input region(s) correspond to output rows and columns;
- whether non-background markers are copied, recolored, aggregated, or filtered;
- how empty/background output cells are determined;
- whether partitions, separator lines, or repeated tiles define independent source regions.

Record the exact source-to-output mapping and check every output cell against multiple pairs. Similar output dimensions alone do not establish the encoding. Before using the rule on a test, derive the output cell-by-cell and verify dimensions. If plausible mappings disagree, use the next demo to distinguish them; do not submit a guessed uniform pattern merely to conserve attempts.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/HA-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/held-out/play/users/u043/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-solving/references/compact-output-interpretation.md"}
